{#
  Shared rendering of vector-store hits for the VegaLiteAgent prompts.

  Included by main, main_altair and revise_output so the three stay in step.
  Example specs live in `metadata.examples` rather than in `text`, deliberately:
  keeping the JSON out of `text` keeps it out of the embedding vector, so a spec
  never dilutes the similarity match. That also means the specs are invisible
  unless rendered here explicitly.

  Specs arrive already normalized to this agent's contract (YAML, no $schema,
  `data: {name: ...}`) -- see scripts/create_vega_lite_docs_embeddings.py.

  The `###` line below already states section and page, and `result.text` carries its
  own `# <page> - <section>` heading, so that line is dropped rather than printed
  twice. Matched by prefix rather than by position: with contextual descriptions
  enabled the heading is no longer the first line, and body markdown only ever uses
  `##` or deeper, so `# ` cannot collide with real content.
#}
{% if doc_pages is defined and doc_pages %}
## Relevant Vega-Lite Documentation (reference specs are illustrative — substitute the real table and column names)

{% for result in doc_pages %}
{%- set body_lines = [] -%}
{%- for line in result.text.split('\n') if not line.startswith('# ') -%}
{%- set _ = body_lines.append(line) -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set body = body_lines | join('\n') | trim -%}
### {{ result.metadata.section_title }} — {{ result.metadata.page_title }}
> Source: {{ result.metadata.url }}

{{ body }}
{% for example in result.metadata.get('examples') or [] %}
Reference spec — {{ example.name }}:
```yaml
{{ example.spec }}
```
{% endfor %}
---
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
